  "title": "How Zep tracks provenance in agent memory",
  "summary": "Agent memory is synthesized: an LLM derives facts from chat histories, documents, and business data. A derived fact matches no source word-for-word, so nothing ties it back to where it came from. Zep records that lineage; debugging, source-scoped retrieval, and compliance all depend on it.",
